recent: 4.5.0-canary.20260504T180558, 4.5.0-canary.20260504T173427, 4.5.0-canary.20260504T173320, 4.5.0-canary.20260504T165552, 4.4.3, 4.5.0-canary.20260504T070434, 4.5.0-canary.20260503T214107, 4.4.2, 4.5.0-canary.20260430T040905, 4.4.1

Per zod@4.4.3:

The `transform` method in Zod v4 is defined by the `$ZodTransformDef` interface, which specifies a `transform` function taking an `input: unknown` and a `payload: ParsePayload<unknown>`, returning `util.MaybeAsync<unknown>`. For piping schemas together, the `$ZodPipeDef` interface defines `transform` and `reverseTransform` optional functions that coerce between the output of the input schema (`A`) and the input of the output schema (`B`).

Source excerpt:
> // v4/core/schemas.d.ts
> export interface $ZodTransformDef extends $ZodTypeDef {
>     type: "transform";
>     transform: (input: unknown, payload: ParsePayload<unknown>) => util.MaybeAsync<unknown>;
> }

